title: Bundestag Elections
new-page: true
tags: event
priority: -1
view-if: (year = next_election_year and month >= next_election_month) or (year > next_election_year)
on-departure: month_actions += 1; in_election = 0; next_election_year = next_election_year + 4; n_elections += 1; next_election_time = time + 48;
set-jump: post_election_1928
face-image: img/Rothe_Wahlen_1903.jpg

# TODO: should there be an image?

# the low priority means that this event is only seen after all other events are resolved for the month.

= Elections, [+ month : month +] [+ year +]

The Bundestag elections are to be held now.

- @election_algorithm: May we do our best...

@post_election_1928
on-arrival: {!
// set old results
// election threshold constitutional reform
// banning parties
var new_party_sum = 0;
for (var party of Q.parties) {
    Q['old_' + party + '_r'] = Q[party + '_r'];
    if (Q[party + '_votes'] < 5 || party == 'other' || Q[party + '_banned']) {
        Q[party + '_r'] = 0;
    } else {
        Q[party + '_r'] = Q[party + '_votes'];
    }
    new_party_sum += Q[party + '_r'];
}
// calculate new party sum if electoral reform
for (var party of Q.parties) {
    if (Q[party + '_r'] > 0) {
        Q[party + '_r'] = Math.round(Q[party + '_r']*1000/new_party_sum)/10;
    }
    Q['change_' + party + '_r'] = Q[party + '_r'] - Q['old_' + party + '_r'];
    var sign = Q['change_' + party + '_r'] > 0 ? '+'  : '';
    Q['str_change_' + party] = sign + Q['change_' + party + '_r'].toFixed(1);
}

// get change arrows and signs


// The largest party can only be the CDU or the SPD.
Q.largest_party = 'SPD';
if (Q.cdu_r >= Q.spd_r) {
    Q.largest_party = 'CDU';
}

// coalitions
Q.social_liberal_coalition = Q.spd_r + Q.fdp_r;
Q.grand_coalition = Q.spd_r + Q.cdu_r;
Q.bourgeois_coalition = Q.fdp_r + Q.cdu_r;

Q.leverage = Q.spd_r;

Q.grand_coalition_failed = 0;
// Reset government and ministers... Based on Brüning's 1930 govt
Q.coalition_dissent = 0;
Q.spd_in_government = 0;
Q.in_grand_coalition = 0;
Q.spd_toleration = 0;
Q.spd_caretaker = 0;

Q.strike_term_seen = 0;

var election_result = {'date': new Date(Q.year, Q.month - 1)};
for (var party of Q.parties) {
    election_result[party] = Q[party + '_r'];
}
Q.election_records.push(election_result);
!}
on-departure:
on-display: {!
data = []
data.push({
      "id": "spd",
      "legend": "SPD",
      "name": "SPD",
      "seats": Math.round(Q.spd_r*5),
});
data.push({
      "id": "fdp",
      "legend": "FDP",
      "name": "FDP",
      "seats": Math.round(Q.fdp_r*5),
});
data.push({
      "id": "cdu",
      "legend": "CDU",
      "name": "CDU",
      "seats": Math.round(Q.cdu_r*5*0.804),
});
data.push({
      "id": "csu",
      "legend": "CSU",
      "name": "CSU",
      "seats": Math.round(Q.cdu_r*5*0.196),
});
data.push({
      "id": "npd",
      "legend": "NPD",
      "name": "NPD",
      "seats": Math.round(Q.npd_r*5),
});
data.push({
      "id": "other",
      "legend": "Other",
      "name": "Other",
      "seats": Math.round(Q.other_r*5),
});

if (window && d3) {
    var width = 500; 
    var height = 500;
    var screenWidth = document.getElementById('content').offsetWidth;
    if (screenWidth < width - 50) {
        width = screenWidth - 50; 
        height = width;
        document.getElementById("reichstag").style.height = screenWidth/2 + "px";
    } 

    var parliament = d3.parliament();
    parliament.width(width).height(height).innerRadiusCoef(0.4);
    parliament.enter.fromCenter(true).smallToBig(true);
    parliament.exit.toCenter(false).bigToSmall(true);
    d3.select("#reichstag").datum(data).call(parliament);
}
!}
go-to: coalition_menu

= Election results

{!<svg id="reichstag" style="width: 500px; height: 250px;"> </svg>!}

{!<table>!} 
{!<tr><td>Party</td><td>Vote share</td><td>% Change</td></tr>!}
{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#C00000; outline: 2px; outline-style: solid;'> </div> !} **SPD:** {!</td><td>!} **[+ spd_r +]%** {!</td><td>!} **[+ str_change_spd +]** {!</td></tr>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#000000'> </div> <div class="box" style='background-color:#286fe0'> </div> !} CDU/CSU: {!</td><td>!} [+ cdu_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_cdu +] {!</td></tr>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#FFCC00'> </div> !} FDP: {!</td><td>!} [+ fdp_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_fdp +] {!</td></tr>!}
 
{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#a0a0a0'> </div> !} Others: {!</td><td>!} [+ other_r +] % {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_other +] {!</td></tr>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#c26f2b'> </div> !} NPD: {!</td><td>!} [+ npd_r +]% {!</td><td>!} [+ str_change_npd +] {!</td></tr>!}
{!</table>!}

**Potential coalitions:**

<span style="color: #C00000;">Social</span>-<span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberal</span> Coalition (<span style="color: #C00000;">**SPD**</span> + <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**FDP**</span>): [+ social_liberal_coalition +]%

<span style="color: #C00000;">Grand</span> <span style="color: #000000;">Coalition</span> (<span style="color: #C00000;">**SPD**</span> + <span style="color: #000000;">**CDU**</span> + <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span>): [+ grand_coalition +]%

<span style="color: #FFCC00;">Bour</span><span style="color: #000000;">geois</span> Coalition (<span style="color: #000000;">**CDU**</span> + <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span> + <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**FDP**</span>): [+ bourgeois_coalition +]%

There are some potential coalition arrangements.

@coalition_menu

- @spd_majority
- @cdu_majority
- @social_liberal_coalition
- @grand_coalition
- @bourgeois_coalition

@cdu_majority
title: A <span style="color: #000000;">**CDU**</span> majority alone
subtitle: <span style="color: #000000;">**CDU**</span>: [+ cdu_r +]%
view-if: cdu_r >= 50
on-arrival: chancellor = "Kiesinger"; chancellor_party = "CDU"; spd_in_government = 0; foreign_minister_party = "CDU"; foreign_minister = "Schröder"; interior_minister_party = "CDU"; interior_minister = "Benda"; justice_minister_party = "CSU"; justice_minister = "Jaeger"; labor_minister_party = "CDU"; labor_minister = "Katzer"; defense_minister_party = "CDU"; defense_minister = "von Hassel"; economic_minister_party = "CDU"; economic_minister = "Schmücker"; finance_minister_party = "CSU"; finance_minister = "Strauß"; agriculture_minister_party = "CSU"; agriculture_minister = "Höcherl";

The <span style="color: #000000;">**CDU**</span>/<span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span> faction has formed a majority government...

@bourgeois_coalition
title: A <span style="color: #FFCC00;">Bour</span><span style="color: #000000;">geois</span> Coalition is formed.
subtitle: <span style="color: #000000;">**CDU**</span> + <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span> + <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**FDP**</span> ([+ bourgeois_coalition +]%)
view-if: bourgeois_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: chancellor = "Kiesinger"; chancellor_party = "CDU"; spd_in_government = 0; foreign_minister_party = "FDP"; foreign_minister = "Genscher"; interior_minister_party = "CDU"; interior_minister = "Benda"; justice_minister_party = "CSU"; justice_minister = "Jaeger"; labor_minister_party = "CDU"; labor_minister = "Katzer"; defense_minister_party = "CDU"; defense_minister = "von Hassel"; economic_minister_party = "CDU"; economic_minister = "Schmücker"; finance_minister_party = "CSU"; finance_minister = "Strauß"; agriculture_minister_party = "CSU"; agriculture_minister = "Höcherl";

For some reason, we cannot or do not want to form a government. This has led to the <span style="color: #000000;">**CDU**</span> forming a coalition with the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**FDP**</span> again.

@spd_majority
title: A <span style="color: #C00000;">**SPD**</span> majority alone
subtitle: <span style="color: #000000;">**SPD**</span>: [+ spd_r +]%
view-if: spd_r >= 50
on-arrival: chancellor = "Empty"; chancellor_party = "SPD"; spd_in_government = 1; in_spd_majority = 1; pro_republic += 5; foreign_minister_party = "SPD"; foreign_minister = "Brandt"; interior_minister_party = "SPD"; interior_minister = "Schmude"; justice_minister_party = "SPD"; justice_minister = "Jahn"; labor_minister_party = "SPD"; labor_minister = "Arendt"; defense_minister_party = "SPD"; defense_minister = "Schmidt"; economic_minister_party = "SPD"; economic_minister = "Schiller"; finance_minister_party = "SPD"; finance_minister = "Möller"; agriculture_minister_party = "SPD"; agriculture_minister = "Engholm"; bundeswehr_loyalty -= 0.05; 
achievement: majority_party

Finally, the <span style="color: #C00000;">**SPD**</span> can govern alone! Our long campaign of electioneering has paid off. We do not need to worry about coalition government; anything is possible. 

Who should be chancellor?

- @brandt_majority_chancellor: Willy Brandt for Chancellor.

@brandt_majority_chancellor
on-arrival: chancellor = "Brandt"

Willy Brandt has become chancellor of the <span style="color: #C00000;">**SPD**</span> majority.

@social_liberal_coalition
title: We can form a <span style="color: #C00000;">Social</span>-<span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberal</span> Coalition.
subtitle: <span style="color: #C00000;">**SPD**</span> + <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**FDP**</span> ([+ social_liberal_coalition +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: [? if fdp_relation < 60: The <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**FDP**</span> does not want to form a coalition with us. ?]
view-if: social_liberal_coalition >= 50 and fdp_relation >= 60
on-arrival: in_social_liberal_coalition = 1; in_grand_coalition = 0; leverage += 5; spd_in_government = 1; foreign_minister_party = "FDP"; interior_minister_party = "FDP"; justice_minister_party = "FDP"; labor_minister_party = "FDP"; defense_minister_party = "FDP"; economic_minister_party = "FDP"; finance_minister_party = "FDP"; agriculture_minister_party = "FDP"; foreign_minister = "Scheel"; interior_minister = "Genscher"; justice_minister = "Logemann"; labor_minister = "Dahrendorf"; defense_minister = "Grüner"; economic_minister = "Friderichs"; finance_minister = "Friderichs"; agriculture_minister = "Ertl";

We have enough votes to form a <span style="color: #C00000;">Social</span>-<span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberal</span> Coalition government consisting of the <span style="color: #C00000;">**SPD**</span> and <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**FDP**</span>!

Who should be the chancellor?

- @brandt

@brandt_coalition_chancellor
title: Willy Brandt for Chancellor
subtitle:
on-arrival: chancellor = "Brandt"; chancellor_party = "SPD";
go-to: ministries

Rudolf Breitscheid has been appointed chancellor.


@grand_coalition
title: We can form a <span style="color: #C00000;">Grand</span> <span style="color: #000000;">Coalition</span>.
view-if: grand_coalition >= 50 and grand_coalition_failed == 0 and cdu_relation >= 60
subtitle: <span style="color: #C00000;">**SPD**</span> + <span style="color: #000000;">**CDU**</span> + <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span> ([+ grand_coalition +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: [? if cdu_relation < 60: The <span style="color: #000000;">**CDU**</span> and <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span> do not want to form a coalition with us. ?]
on-arrival: in_grand_coalition = 1;
go-to: grand_coalition_spd_lead if largest_party == "SPD"; grand_coalition_cdu_lead if largest_party == "CDU"

@grand_coalition_cdu_lead
view-if: grand_coalition >= 50
on-arrival: spd_in_government = 1; spd_toleration = 0; in_grand_coalition = 1; chancellor = "Kiesinger"; chancellor_party = "CDU"; foreign_minister_party = "DVP"; interior_minister_party = "Z"; justice_minister_party = "Z"; labor_minister_party = "Z"; defense_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister_party = "Z"; finance_minister_party = "Z"; agriculture_minister_party = "Z"; leverage = 25 if leverage >= 25;
go-to: ministries

We can form a <span style="color: #C00000;">Grand</span> <span style="color: #000000;">Coalition</span> with the <span style="color: #000000;">**CDU**</span> and <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span>. The Union has more votes than us and gets the chancellory.

@grand_coalition_spd_lead
on-arrival: leverage -= 15; in_grand_coalition = 1

We can form a <span style="color: #C00000;">Grand</span> <span style="color: #000000;">Coalition</span> with the <span style="color: #000000;">**CDU**</span> and <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span>. We have more votes than the Union and get the chancellory.

Who should be the chancellor?

- @brandt


@brandt
title: Willy Brandt for Chancellor
subtitle:
on-arrival: spd_in_government = 1; chancellor = "Brandt"; chancellor_party = "SPD"
go-to: ministries

Willy Brandt is voted Chancellor.

@ministries

We can pick from any number of ministries. Controlling a ministry allows us to directly effect policy in that area.

- #mins_1928
- #drop_mins_1928

@labor
title: Labor Ministry
subtitle: Taking the Labor Ministry is expected of us.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1928
choose-if: leverage >= 5
view-if: labor_minister_party != "SPD"
on-arrival: leverage -= 5; labor_minister_party = "SPD"; labor_minister = "Arendt"
go-to: ministries

Walter Arendt of the SPD has been appointed labor minister.

@interior
title: Interior Ministry
subtitle: Taking the Interior Ministry is expected of us. The Interior Ministry controls domestic security.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1928
choose-if: leverage >= 5
view-if: interior_minister_party != "SPD"
on-arrival: leverage -= 5; interior_minister_party = "SPD"; interior_minister = "Schmude"
go-to: ministries

Jürgen Schmude of the SPD has been appointed Interior Minister.

@finance
title: Finance Ministry
subtitle: The Finance Ministry controls the government budget and taxes.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1928
choose-if: leverage >= 10 
view-if: finance_minister_party != "SPD"
on-arrival: leverage -= 10; finance_minister_party = "SPD"; finance_minister = "Möller"
go-to: ministries

Alex Möller of the SPD has been appointed Finance Minister.

@economic
title: Economic Ministry
subtitle: The Economic Ministry controls broader economic policy.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1928
choose-if: leverage >= 10 
view-if: economic_minister_party != "SPD"
on-arrival: leverage -= 10; economic_minister_party = "SPD"; economic_minister = "Schiller"
go-to: ministries

Karl Schiller of the SPD has been appointed Economic Minister.

@justice
title: Justice Ministry
subtitle: The Justice Ministry controls the courts.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1928
choose-if: leverage >= 10 
view-if: justice_minister_party != "SPD"
on-arrival: leverage -= 10; justice_minister_party = "SPD"; justice_minister = "Jahn"
go-to: ministries

Gerhard Jahn of the SPD has been appointed Justice Minister.

@foreign
title: Foreign Ministry
subtitle: The foreign ministry controls our foreign affairs.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1928
choose-if: leverage >= 10 
view-if: foreign_minister_party != "SPD"
on-arrival: leverage -= 10; foreign_minister_party = "SPD"; foreign_minister = "Brandt"
go-to: ministries

Willy Brandt of the SPD has been appointed Foreign Minister.


@agriculture
title: Agricultural Ministry
subtitle: This is not our usual domain.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
choose-if: leverage >= 10 
view-if: agriculture_minister_party != "SPD"
on-arrival: leverage -= 10; agriculture_minister_party = "SPD"; agriculture_minister = "Engholm"
go-to: ministries
tags: mins_1928

Björn Engholm of the SPD has been appointed Agriculture Minister.

@defense
title: Defense Ministry
subtitle: The Ministry responsible for the armed forces is not typically our domain.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have enough leverage.
tags: mins_1928
choose-if: leverage >= 10 
view-if: defense_minister_party != "SPD"
on-arrival: leverage -= 10; defense_minister_party = "SPD"; defense_minister = "Schmidt"
go-to: ministries

Helmut Schmidt of the SPD has been appointed Defense Minister.



@no_more
title: No more ministries.
subtitle: [? if leverage >= 10 : We still have some more leverage to gain ministries. ?][? if leverage < 10 : We do not have much leverage left. ?]
tags: mins_1928

This coalition arrangement is tolerable to all.

@drop_labor
title: Drop the Labor Ministry.
view-if: labor_minister_party = "SPD"
on-arrival: labor_minister_party = "FDP" if in_social_liberal_coalition; labor_minister_party = "CDU" if in_grand_coalition; labor_minister = "Dahrendorf" if in_social_liberal_coalition; labor_minister = "Katzer" if in_grand_coalition; leverage += 5
tags: drop_mins_1928
go-to: ministries

